From: =?UTF-8?q?L=C6=B0u=20Oa=20Oa?=
 <212658678+luuoaoa@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 15:52:53 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Vietnamese IME: deliver Telex settings live on the mojo
 rule-based path

The UnikeyEngine (and the recovered rule-based engine) only ever saw their
settings at connect time, so the os-settings Vietnamese toggles were inert:
switching "new-style tone placement" did not flip hoaf between hoa-grave and
hoa-modern without a full IME reconnect. Two latent bugs plus a missing focus
hop were responsible (VIETNAMESE-IME-PERF.md sec 4.3):

1. CreateSettingsFromPrefs matched only "vkd_vi_telex", but the rule-based mojo
   path connects with the normalized "m17n:vi_telex" spec, so the Vietnamese
   settings union was silently never built and the engine came up with defaults.
   Normalize the m17n: spec back to the vkd_ id for both the predicate match and
   the per-input-method pref sub-dictionary lookup.

2. RuleBasedEngine::OnFocus reported success=false, which (via OnFocusAck) would
   have marked the text client inactive and dropped CommitText/SetComposition
   once focus was actually delivered on this path. Report success.

3. The observer routed rule-based focus/options changes only to the component
   extension, never to the mojo engine, so OnFocus settings never reached it.
   Deliver a fresh per-focus settings snapshot to the mojo engine on the
   rule-based path (without making the text-client active-state depend on its
   reply, so no other vkd_* layout regresses), and re-deliver it live when the
   focused field's options change (OnInputMethodOptionsChanged) so a toggle
   takes effect with no re-focus and no reconnect.

UnikeyEngine now consumes the full Telex settings union: modern/classic tone
placement (D1), flexible diacritics (freeMarking), and the composition-underline
pref; it commits any in-flight preedit before re-applying settings mid-word.

VERIFIED on device (colorburst R153, instance 2, owner imetail): with Telex
active in a textarea, hoaf -> "hoa-grave"; flip new-style in os-settings with the
field still focused (no refocus, no reconnect) and hoaf -> "hoa-modern"; flip
back and it returns to "hoa-grave".



